	(text
		"DESIGN NOTES\nLD2410B 24 GHz radar on J3 at the board edge, antenna facing the front cover; no copper under the antenna.\nOUT (pin1, 3.3 V) -> PB4: HIGH = person present. UART TX/RX on J4 for the Hi-Link PC config tool (3.3 V).\nSW1 override on PB2 (debounced, 1k series so it does not fight the ISP SCK). RP1 10k pull-up, active low.\nRV1 10k trimmer -> ADC3 sets the no-one OFF delay (10 s ... 10 min, mapped in firmware).\nD1 status LED on PB1: on = presence, slow blink = manual mode, fast blink = fault (e.g. radar not responding)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 62.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aed23466-2553-551f-a0f4-d87a986fd67e")
	)
	(text
		"PART NOTES (VERIFY = check against vendor datasheet before release)\nJ3: Keep the antenna end clear of copper (no pour under it) and of metal in the lid. OUT high = presence.\nC4: local decoupling at the radar header\nRP1: button pull-up (active-low)\nCB2: debounce; on the switch side, not on SCK\nRS2: series into PB2/SCK; isolates the button during ISP\nRL1: LED current ~ (5-2)/1k = 3 mA\nC6: ADC filter on the wiper"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 219.71 62.23 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "75724261-05d5-5ca4-a2e9-c1efe393fc1b")
	)
)
